{"text": " What does a breach actually cost you? Not a red, amber, green dot on a dashboard, a number in pounds. Most governance ignores that, compliant or not, a green tick that price nothing and move nothing, a binary lie. But here's the idea, governance is not a checkbox. It is a proportionate, continuously retuned response to quantified risk, and it is all one thing, the policy, how your organization actually operates, written down as code. Start where your engineers already live. Policy is just a dependency, a lint pack. You pin it, you sign it, you adopt it by pull request. Governance becomes something a developer already knows how to consume and trust. Now, the moment that makes it land, two institutions, a retailer and a hospital. Same platform, same engine, one identical rule, encrypt data at rest. Watch what proportionality actually does to that single control. In the retailer, it merely audits. In the hospital, the very same rule blocks. Why? Because a health breach costs far more, so the model prices it far higher. Same control, opposite verdict, because the pounds say so. But real governance is never just yes or no. Fall behind on patching and your workload still runs but caged, throttled, sandboxed, watched more closely, least trusted, most expensive to run. A spectrum of consequence, not a cliff edge, and that cage costs money while still leaving risk behind. So staying current becomes provably the cheaper path. Add it up, the risk you keep plus the cost of every control. That is your true total cost of risk. These pounds are real, not guessed. Calibrated estimates, a Monte Carlo simulation, and the tail your board actually fears the insurance industry's own maths. Tighten the control, the number falls. Accept a risk, it rises. Live on screen. So we kill the ugliest word in governance. Exemption, no carve outs, no favors. Instead, you may do this if you meet these conditions. Uniform version priced. Every allowance carries its own honest line of accepted risk. Here's the leap. The policy version you satisfy becomes your identity. Every workload, every person, every device carries it cryptographically. A sensitive service simply refuses anyone who has fallen out of date. Zero trust, finally made real. Failures move left. The cluster advertises which policy versions it accepts. Your pipeline runs the exact check the cluster will offline before you merge. A deploy time surprise becomes practically unheard of. The compliant path becomes the easy path. Then it comes alive, the estate war games itself. Threat feeds, new vulnerabilities, regulator fines, all pour in. An agent stress tests your controls and asks one question, is this still proportionate or has the world quietly moved? When it drifts, the agent does exactly one thing. It opens a pull request. It proposes, it never disposes. A human reviews, the gate checks, and only then does it ship. A powerful machine safe on your existing rails. And every actor, human or machine, signs their work. Cryptographically signed, publicly logged, verifiable end to end. You can prove which actor changed what, when, and from what evidence for an AI-enabled business. That is how you trust it. So what does your funding build? Six real organizations brought to life a shared platform. Three institutions, two regulators publishing controls and fines as code. A cluster each where every core claim is demonstrated, not slideware. And here's why this is ours to build. Flux is not a logo on a slide. It is load-bearing, doing six real jobs, distribution, provenance, pruning, healing, ordering, alerts. This puts Flux at the very center of the risk story, which lets us close where no security talk ever closes, the balance sheet. Residual risk becomes economic capital. The very same controls an underwriter would price. Technological risk, finally, a line your board can read, defend and act on. For the spend, you get three things that compound. A flagship talk that tours every conference, a demo estate our teams put in front of any prospect, and ownership of a story no competitor in this market is telling yet. And the timing is the whole point. Every board is asking how to trust AI inside their business. We answer it provably, on stage, in pounds. Whoever tells this story first owns it, and that window is open right now. So here's the ask. Fund the full build every step through to the flagship talk. Give me that runway. And I'll hand you the estate that proves governance can finally be proportionate, honest, and alive. Let's put risk on the balance sheet.", "segments": [{"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.08, "text": " What does a breach actually cost you?", "tokens": [50363, 1867, 857, 257, 13694, 1682, 1575, 345, 30, 50467], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 2.08, "end": 4.8, "text": " Not a red, amber, green dot on a dashboard,", "tokens": [50467, 1892, 257, 2266, 11, 36505, 11, 4077, 16605, 319, 257, 30415, 11, 50603], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 4.8, "end": 6.48, "text": " a number in pounds.", "tokens": [50603, 257, 1271, 287, 8059, 13, 50687], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 4, "seek": 0, "start": 6.48, "end": 10.24, "text": " Most governance ignores that, compliant or not,", "tokens": [50687, 4042, 18848, 24245, 326, 11, 31332, 393, 407, 11, 50875], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 5, "seek": 0, "start": 10.24, "end": 12.74, "text": " a green tick that price nothing and move nothing,", "tokens": [50875, 257, 4077, 4378, 326, 2756, 2147, 290, 1445, 2147, 11, 51000], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 6, "seek": 0, "start": 12.74, "end": 13.92, "text": " a binary lie.", "tokens": [51000, 257, 13934, 6486, 13, 51059], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 7, "seek": 0, "start": 13.92, "end": 16.7, "text": " But here's the idea, governance is not a checkbox.", "tokens": [51059, 887, 994, 338, 262, 2126, 11, 18848, 318, 407, 257, 2198, 3524, 13, 51198], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 8, "seek": 0, "start": 16.7, "end": 20.080000000000002, "text": " It is a proportionate, continuously retuned response", "tokens": [51198, 632, 318, 257, 9823, 378, 11, 17282, 1005, 40881, 2882, 51367], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 9, "seek": 0, "start": 20.080000000000002, "end": 23.02, "text": " to quantified risk, and it is all one thing,", "tokens": [51367, 284, 5554, 1431, 2526, 11, 290, 340, 318, 477, 530, 1517, 11, 51514], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 10, "seek": 0, "start": 23.02, "end": 26.48, "text": " the policy, how your organization actually operates,", "tokens": [51514, 262, 2450, 11, 703, 534, 4009, 1682, 14051, 11, 51687], "avg_logprob": -0.10960374981903832, "compression_ratio": 1.6245353159851301, "no_speech_prob": 0.0008104061707854271, "words": null, "temperature": 0.0}, {"id": 11, "seek": 0, "start": 26.48, "en